  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2; Task full execution; Redesign from First Principles; Plate Plan adoption; Best API doctrine repair; Verify Plate package/browser/native proof; Benchmark production proof; Plate Docs; Maintain Workflow; Agent Native Reviewer closure audit",
  "trigger": "The user accepted the final retained-source plan and authorized direct full Task execution after the DOCX OSS reassessment.",
  "requirements": [
    "Keep semantic DOCX conversion as the zero-retention default and add source lifetime only through an explicit import opt-in.",
    "Make source availability exact in TypeScript: literal true success owns a source, default and false success do not, dynamic booleans require narrowing, and callers cannot construct a valid source.",
    "Retain the admitted immutable Blob without another compressed-byte copy, deep-clone and freeze the semantic/comment baseline, bind the complete schema identity and limits, and expose only idempotent disposal.",
    "Return original bytes only for the same complete schema, unchanged review document, review projection, unchanged or unspecified comments, and no explicit package metadata or page-layout override.",
    "After edits, regenerate the complete main document and preserve only relationship-closed safe root or one-section header/footer graphs; never splice unproved body XML.",
    "Omit active content, signatures, external relationships, conflicts, unreachable parts and ambiguous multi-section headers or footers with structured diagnostics and final bounded package validation.",
    "Keep source bytes outside Plite, EditorDocumentValue, editor plugins, comments storage and persistence; the first-party app owns replacement, disposal and explicit export pairing.",
    "Adopt current docs, JSDoc, registry source and generated output, package boundaries, changeset and doctrine, then prove focused behavior, public types, packed consumers, Chromium, LibreOffice and frozen four-cohort performance."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reused the accepted retained-source Best API reviews, the 2026-09-15 OSS packet and its source-identity/invalidation findings, the canonical semantic converter proof, and the pre-acceptance frozen budgets only where their requirements remained unchanged. Rechecked the final public types, source lifetime, bounded package owner, exact path, edited relationship overlay, app provider/toolbars, English and Chinese docs, generated registry, packed entrypoints, browser workflow, LibreOffice render/re-save/reimport, production benchmark, doctrine source and generated mirrors in the current checkout.",
  "summary": "Pursue and mark adopted. DOCX import can explicitly retain one opaque disposable DocxSource; unchanged review export returns the original Blob only after complete schema, document, comment, projection and option checks. Edited export regenerates the body and overlays safe relationship-closed root and one-section header/footer graphs while diagnosing every rewrite or omission class. Default conversion retains no source, the app owns lifetime, Plite remains unchanged, and package, browser, LibreOffice and production performance proof pass.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-15-documents-retained-source-final-reassessment",
  "relation": "reaffirms",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep diagnostics-only semantic conversion: reject for the first-party import-edit-export job because unrelated source package content is lost even when Plate never owned it.",
    "Retain the complete ZIP or place source bytes in editor/plugin state: reject because it hides tens of megabytes, disposal, persistence boundaries, source pairing and active-content risk.",
    "Add DocxSession, a second importer/exporter or a public OOXML model: reject because no independent editing command lifecycle exists and feature serializers retain separate owners.",
    "Patch paragraph or run XML after edits: defer because current correspondence cannot prove relationship, style, numbering, comment, revision and resource remapping under structural changes.",
    "Use one typed opt-in DocxSource with exact no-op reuse and coarse relationship-closed overlay: selected and implemented because it preserves provable source behavior without weakening the canonical semantic document or default path."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Microsoft Word certification, arbitrary package-preserving edits, paragraph/run XML retention after body edits, body media ingestion, notes, fields, multi-section header/footer reconstruction, persistent source reattachment, collaboration transport and external repository suites are not claimed. LibreOffice proves readability and native re-save, not Word-equivalent layout. Chromium proof is Chromium-only. The aggregate registry test remains outside this scoped proof because concurrent untracked rich-text registry work changes its expected file list; focused DOCX registry tests, generated registry/source parity and website typecheck pass. No commit, push, PR, release or publication is claimed.",
